# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# pulseMask_Tech — what does NOT go to the public GitHub repo.
#
# This repo is the live site, so anything committed here is published. The split
# below is "would I be happy for a customer or a competitor to read this?".
# Nothing here is a credential — there are none in this project. It is business
# strategy, internal process, and local machine state.
#
# To publish something again, delete its line and `git add -f` it.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Commercially sensitive ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Unlaunched pricing, per-unit cost breakdown, margins and capacity.
docs/founder-run.stash.md
# Internal legal posture: personal liability, LLC/DBA reasoning, tax exposure.
docs/licensing.md
# Payment-processor setup, tax decisions, price-change plans, and the format
# used to mint PMK- unlock codes.
zookah.todos.md

# Catch anything else dropped into docs/ — it is the internal-notes folder.
# Re-publish individual files with `git add -f docs/<file>`.
docs/

# ── Internal engineering + process docs ──────────────────────────────────────
# Useful to me and to agents, not to visitors. HANDOFF.md in particular spells
# out that the export gate is a soft storefront gate rather than DRM, and both
# it and the playbook describe unshipped work.
HANDOFF.md
VSCODE.md
AGENT_PLAYBOOK.md
CLAUDE.md
CLAUDE_DESIGN_BUNDLE.md

